# LoopPlane environment variables — example.
# Copy to `.env` and edit as needed. The smallest run needs NONE of these:
# by default LoopPlane uses a built-in, credential-free demo model (no network,
# no keys). `.env` itself is gitignored.

# --- Real model (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# Opt in to a real model by naming an importable "module:function" reference — a
# zero-argument callable that returns a `loopplane.model.ModelBoundary`. An unset
# or bad reference safely falls back to the demo model. See
# `src/loopplane/cli/providers.py`. You write the builder, e.g.:
#   LOOPPLANE_MODEL=mypackage.models:build_claude

# --- Provider credentials (optional) -----------------------------------------
# LoopPlane never reads these directly; the provider SDKs pick them up from the
# environment when your builder constructs an adapter without injecting an
# api_key (`loopplane.adapters.anthropic` / `loopplane.adapters.openai`).
# Install the matching extra first, e.g. `pip install ".[anthropic]"`.
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Point the OpenAI adapter at any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (vLLM, a gateway, a
# self-hosted server); the OpenAI SDK reads this automatically. Use the URL up to
# `/v1` (the part before `/chat/completions`).
#   OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://your-openai-compatible-host/v1

# --- Observability (optional) ------------------------------------------------
# Set an OTLP endpoint to enable the OpenTelemetry overlay/export; leave unset to
# keep observability off.
#   OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
